{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794045842,"nonce":"pFf671mCY/oiYln0OaVMp/b948E=","title":"Rayzor 2: run a reduced signal/effect graph for memory behaviour","message":"Part of b44662d (ashui on Rayzor).\n\nRayzor has no GC. Run a reduced version of ashui's reactive graph (signals, computeds, effects holding closures, an owner tree with a parent/child cycle) on Rayzor and check for leaks, aliasing and use-after-free. rayzor-a3: closure captures count as escaping; retaining callees, statics and non-variable right-hand sides have uncovered paths, one confirmed aliasing bug. The result decides whether reactive state stays in the native plugin. Blocks Rayzor 4.","files":null}]}